{"ts":"2026-08-09T18:03:52.179Z","type":"finding","frontier":"raft-committed-prefix-conflict-livelock-main","claim":"Hot-failure-path live A/B complete (N=4 fixed vs N=6 no-fix control, 3-node examples-catalog boots): livelock ENGAGEMENT PROVEN — max repeat of any single (requestedIndex,committedIndex) refusal pair is 2 across all four fixed runs (reports ec-abfix-20260809T17*) vs 302x/363x single-index wedges pre-fix; remaining refusals are the benign transient-churn class that also appears in passing runs (62 refusals in the PASSing run 3). HONEST CORRECTIONS: (1) boot pass rate did NOT improve (fixed 1/4 vs control 3/6 — statistically indistinguishable); the flake's root is elsewhere — joiner joining:readiness-convergence duration is BIMODAL (~5ms when placement already satisfied vs full 120s timeout when waiting; one green run had a joiner burn the full 120862ms and still recover), i.e. a spread-wait race, successor-quest territory. (2) The new COMMITTED_PREFIX_DIVERGENCE event fired zero times in all four fixed runs — the poisoned-prefix state did not arise; wedge-free reds exist, so the earlier dominant-face claim overstated causality (refusal spam correlated with reds pre-fix but a second requester, the base append-mismatch truncation, produces transient refusals in green runs too).","kind":null,"evidence":"test-output/reports/ec-abfix-20260809T175516Z.report.json","rulesOut":null,"verification":null,"regressionClassification":null,"scopePressureClassification":null}
